A.compiling
1.to compile the application successfully, you need to clone AppProtocols(git@codeup.aliyun.com:6347c4cf0e55ca746598185e/FirmwareAcrhitecture/AppProtocols.git) into skf_gw first;

B
1.about library pthread, ref@git://git.savannah.gnu.org/hurd/libpthread.git for more info    


2. sometimes the compiling warning may cause deadly problem, so fix all warning is a good habbit

3.about library ell, you can clone it from git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/libs/ell/ell.git . ref@https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/libs/ell/ell.git/  for more info
 NOTE!!!a. the commit we are using is 	11c1f40a77c7d9d9cf7a29ae1d91dab374e5e90c . you can update to the latest version.ref@ell_commit_applied.png
        b.commands for compiling ell-library ref@command_to_compile_ell_for_forlinx.txt	


4.about OK6231-C_0621B.dtb
Device tree which support the gateway user-key  
how to use ?
a. replace /boot/OK6231-C.dtb by this dtb.
b. then reboot
c. /dev/input/by-path/platform-mcu-gpio-keys-event is expected to be seen and we can see the GPIO is registered by command "cat /sys/kernel/debug/gpio"  
	when the dtb is replaced successfully
d.run "evtest /dev/input/by-path/by-path/platform-gpio-keys-event"
	then press the key, we an see the key-event is detected

5.OK6231-C_with_led_key_support.dtb
	device tree which supports led and key 


6.to add support for BT advertising interval modification
 to support this feature, you need to modify /etc/init.d/bluetooth to run bluetoothd with option "-E"
 FYI:   "/usr/libexec/bluetooth/bluetoothd &"   =>  "/usr/libexec/bluetooth/bluetoothd -E &"





